WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.769
 Well, Paul, Isaac,
congratulations.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:06.072
You are both moving forward into
round three of our competition.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.640
Now, you guys are heading
back to your home forges

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.512
to work on yet another iconic
weapon from the Civil War era.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:13.946
And that weapon is

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.516
[music playing]

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:21.954
Ulysses Grant's Donelson sword.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.490
[music playing]

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.959
 The Donelson sword is a
commemorative blade awarded

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:29.429
to General Ulysses S
Grant for his victory

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.799
at Fort Donelson in
February of 1862,

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:36.235
one of the first major Union
victories of the Civil War.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:38.104
The weapon features a
highly ornate handle

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.874
and an engraved blade based
on the popular 1860s officer

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.342
sword.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.779
After General Grant's death,
his wife donated the sword

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.281
to the Smithsonian
Institute in 1886,

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:51.851
and it remains under
their care to this day.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.487
 You have four days
to work on your swords.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.454
Good luck.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:56.456
See you then.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.458
[music playing]

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:04.130 line:8%
 I'm Isaac Gardner,
and I'm 24 years old.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.565 line:14%
I'm a full-time jeweler.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.768
As a jeweler, there's a
lot of small detail work

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.536
and making sure that
I have something

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:13.605
that's one, comfortable,
and two, strong, and three,

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.041
looks amazing.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:18.744
So as a bladesmith I focus
on the same three aspects.

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:20.913
It's time to quench it.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.750
Oh, OK.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.719
Hopefully, it came out hard.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:27.586
That's hard.

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:28.955
That's hard.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.357
Oh, I feel so much better.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:36.563
I need the rear-facing quillon,
and the two clamshell guards,

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.197
and the knuckle bow.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.565
It's going to be
something like that.

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:42.235
So now that I have the
components complete

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:44.403
I can move on to
welding them together.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.906
I'm really happy with
how it's looking.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:50.142
That's so cool.

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:52.778
It's really ornate and complex.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:57.883
I cut in the channels for my
turquoise and amber inlay.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:58.884
There we go.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.152
Cool beans.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:01.721
I've worked really
hard up to this point,

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:07.427
and now I'm so happy with my
General Grant's Donelson sword.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.663 line:14%
[music playing]

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.965 line:14%
 I'm Paul Sutt.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.334 line:8%
I'm from New Jersey and
I'm a personal trainer.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:19.105
So I've been a lifelong martial
artist and a weapons expert.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:22.341
And when I had the opportunity
to learn how to forge,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.077
I jumped on it as
fast as I could.

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.546
It's just my passion.

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:29.281
So we're getting
close to quench time.

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.183
It's a little tricky for
me because I've never

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.085
done a blade this thin before.

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:34.554
I'm nervous as hell.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.924
Two whole days hammering
this sword out.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.826
If something goes
wrong with the quench

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.960
there is no time
to do that again.

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:42.795
Here we go.

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:48.000
Don't feel any tings
or pings or anything.

00:02:48.066 --> 00:02:50.769
I pull it out and I'm so happy.

00:02:50.869 --> 00:02:51.638
It looks straight.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.939
It looks perfect.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.642
So now I'm going to do a little
bit of work on the clamshell,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.411
try to make it look as pretty
as I can as quick as I can.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.813
And then it's going to
be shaping the handle

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.581
into a comfortable handle.

00:03:02.681 --> 00:03:03.783
Almost.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.586
So I finally got all the
pieces to fit on the tang.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:07.720
All right.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.056
This entire experience
has been more fun than I

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:12.458
ever imagined it would be.

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:17.229
The blade is a little bit
chunky, but it will kill.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:19.765
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.735
The sword is made to be
a dueling type of weapon.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:25.671
So I'm going to try to
deliver the same light slashes

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:28.240
and thrust to this
ballistics dummy.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:29.608
Paul, you ready for this?

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.576
 Oh yes, sir.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.143
 All right.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:31.911
Let's do this.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.581
[music playing]

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.736
 All right, Paul.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.738
Let's talk about your version of
General Grant's Donelson sword.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:03.642
The weight on this blade is
not that of a dueling sword

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:08.214
because it requires a little bit
more than just wrist movement.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.683
But it is a great cutting sword.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.752
Your edges are sharp.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:15.721
Even with the harassing cut you
can see they're cutting deeply.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:20.326
And more importantly,
sir, it will kill.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.193
Isaac, your turn, sir.

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:22.061
Are you ready for this?

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.029
 I guess.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:24.096
 OK.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.766
[music playing]

00:04:43.348 --> 00:04:44.350
 All right, Isaac.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:45.685
Let's talk about
your weapon here.

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.286
What I like about
it is the time you

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:50.055
took to put these
details that we were

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:52.692
asking for onto your sword.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:54.693
Every cut was deep.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.229
And not a lot of power
is required when you're

00:04:57.296 --> 00:04:58.798
swinging something so light.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:02.702
But, probably hitting
the bone, your blade

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:06.238
did take a slight bend.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:09.975
But overall, sir,
your weapon will kill.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:10.709
 Thank you.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.313
[music playing]

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:16.482
 Paul, Isaac, you
know what time it is.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.817
Time for the strength test.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:22.221
A fan favorite and the
cringe-worthy flex test.

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.389
And we're going to
flex those blades to 35

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:25.824
degrees in either direction.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:28.093
If you're still holding
true, we're going to go to 45

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.463
degrees in either direction.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.630
Paul, you ready for this?

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.400
 Not really, but go
ahead and bend away.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.670
[music playing]

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.595
 Oh!

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:03.429
 Oh.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:11.437
[music playing]

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:14.406
 So Paul, as far as the
construction of your blade

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:16.141
goes, the handle's
comfortable, we

00:06:16.241 --> 00:06:18.244
saw how will this sword cuts.

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.445
You did a good job.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.847
But if you look
into that blade, you

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.618
can actually see a dark spot
on both sides of this blade.

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:28.621
And whether that's a
flaw that you picked up

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:31.690
in the forging process
or flaw in the steel,

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.826
I have no way of really
telling right now.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.794
The grain structure
on this looks fine.

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:39.098
But having it shatter,
having it pop like that,

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:40.199
that's a big issue.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.233
 Mm-hmm.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.937
[music playing]

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.141
 Well Paul, we absolutely
hate to see that.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:50.076
You put a lot of
work into your blade.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:52.812
You made it past
35 on both sides,

00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:54.847
but you did break
on the way to 45.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.615
But you're not out
of the fight yet.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:59.652
Isaac, you've got to survive
both of the 35 degree turns

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:04.456
as well as the official ruling
of 40 degrees towards south.

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:06.692
 My heart is in my throat.

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:09.729
This is literally make or break.

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:13.433
[music playing]

00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:41.893
 Congratulations, man.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.262
 Thanks.

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:46.866
[music playing]

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.736
 Paul, I want to say thank
you for your hard work.

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:52.671
You have what it takes
to fight in this forge.

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:54.640
But, unfortunately, I'm going
to have to ask you to please

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.174
step off the forge floor.

00:07:56.241 --> 00:07:57.743
 Thank you, gentlemen.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.345
This was such a good experience
and it was an honor to compete

00:08:00.445 --> 00:08:02.080
against such a good competitor.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.850
 Isaac we asked you to build
General Grant's Donelson sword.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:08.488
You performed phenomenally and
built us something that is not

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:11.390
only functional but absolutely
beautiful and stunning

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.625
to look at.

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:14.960
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.563
and you, sir, earned
yourself a check for $10,000.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:18.864
Congratulations.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.000
 I'm the "Forged in
Fire" champion, baby!

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.236
Woo!

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:24.903
 How do you feel?

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.038
 Cloud nine.

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:27.173
Feeling so good.

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:28.807
 That's a remarkable
piece of work

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:30.876
and you should be
incredibly proud of it.

00:08:30.976 --> 00:08:31.877
 Thank you.

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:33.379
There's just too
many feelings going

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:36.749
through my head and my
heart to really process

00:08:36.815 --> 00:08:39.051
what's all happening right now.

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:39.986
I can't believe it.

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.319
I'm feeling so good.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:44.290
[music playing]

